From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:38:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerVideo: keep a held picture until the renderer
 takes it

A held picture waits for the renderer while only priority messages are
served, but any priority message (a speed change at resume) ended that
wait. The next packet then released the picture unrendered; on Amlogic
that drops every older queued frame and video runs ahead of audio.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
@@ -0,7 +0,8 @@
     MsgQueueReturnCode ret = GetMessage(pMsg, timeout, iPriority);
 
     const bool drainPending = drainWait;
-    onlyPrioMsgs = false;
+    // a packet decoded over a held picture releases it unrendered
+    onlyPrioMsgs = m_outputSate == OUTPUT_AGAIN && m_picture.videoBuffer;
     drainWait = false;
 
     if (MSGQ_IS_ERROR(ret))
